  "scientific_conclusion": [
    "Conditioning the physical residual marginal on the scalar V14 backbone is strongly supported: it reduces every frozen extreme-tail diagnostic in every domain by a large factor.",
    "The scalar backbone value is nevertheless not a sufficient local condition. TNG100 and SIMBA still miss 2PCF morphology, while Swift still misses ensemble coverage, and all three exceed Q3/Q4 limits.",
    "The next representation must consume oriented local galaxy-count and radial-velocity patches plus multiscale backbone context; another unconditional likelihood, A(k), clipping, or scalar-bin refinement is not justified.",
